course: dictionary
lesson: 11542
title: Ambient: the world around us
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ambient is a word about surroundings. It means the things already around you, in the place where you are. «The ambient temperature in the classroom was 20 degrees.» That is the temperature of the air around us, so ambient means around.
explain: Look at the words near it for clues. «The ambient noise of traffic filled the room.» The traffic noise was already there, not made by you, so ambient describes sound that is all around. Ask: what word would fit here? Try "the noise around us" and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Ambient can also describe music. «The café played soft ambient music while we ate.» Ambient music is quiet and gentle, made to create a calm mood, not to be listened to closely. The words around it tell you which meaning is meant.
fact: Ambient means in the surroundings, around you.
fact: «Ambient temperature» means the temperature of the air around us, often room temperature.
fact: «Ambient light» is the light already there, such as daylight in a room.
fact: «Ambient noise» is the sound already around you, such as traffic or chatter.
fact: Ambient music is quiet, gentle music made to create a calm mood.
exercise: «The ambient temperature in the classroom was 20 degrees.» What does ambient mean here? | Very hot | *Of the air around us | Cold and wet | Written on the board
exercise: «The café played soft ambient music while we ate.» What kind of music is this? | Music sung by a choir | *Quiet, gentle music for a calm mood | Music played in a school hall | Loud dance music for a party
exercise: Which phrase means the sound already around you, such as traffic? | *ambient noise | ambient music | ambient light | ambient temperature
test: «The ambient light from the window made the room bright.» What does ambient light mean? | Light from a torch | *The light already around us | Light that makes a loud noise | A light you switch on yourself
test: In «ambient temperature», what does ambient mean? | *Around us | Lowest possible | Hidden inside something | Very high
exam: «The ambient noise of the city faded as we walked into the quiet park.» What does ambient noise mean? | Music played by a band | *Sounds already around us | A noise made by a bell | Silence
